What is Git?

Git is a distributed version control system used to:

track code changes

manage project versions

collaborate with developers

It allows developers to work efficiently and safely.

Git is preferred over older VCS tools like SVN, CVS, etc., because it is:

✅ Distributed
✅ Fast
✅ Reliable
✅ Supports branching easily
✅ Works offline
✅ Widely used in industry

✅  Better Collaboration

Git allows:

multiple developers working simultaneously

easy merging

conflict handling

pull requests (via GitHub)

Perfect for team projects.

✅  Data Integrity & Safety

Git uses SHA hashing to protect data.

✔ detects corruption
✔ tracks every change
✔ ensures code safety

🚀 Simple Real-Life Example (VERY IMPORTANT)
👨‍💻 Scenario: You and Your Friend Working on Project

You are building your Library Management System.

🔴 Using Old VCS (like SVN)

Suppose:

You edit login code

Your friend edits database code

Server crashes ❌

👉 Entire work is stuck
👉 Risk of losing data
👉 Must wait for server

🟢 Using Git

Both of you have full repo locally.

Even if:

❌ GitHub is down
❌ Internet is off